module test.claim.extdeps_scope_placement_gate_live_wet_witness

// THE ENROLMENT ATTEMPT FOR gunbc.instruments.extdeps_scope_placement_gate (roadmap node
// dp-m3-extdeps-scope-halved, gunbc#15583). What this module does NOT claim, stated first because
// the repository's own ledger (gunbc.recurring_failure_mode::consumer_relies_on_incidental_realization_property,
// and the 2026-10-01 note this change deletes) is a history of exactly this sentence being asserted
// before it was measured: as of this change NO RUN HAS EXECUTED THE CLAIM BELOW. The fleet is down
// fleet-wide (a session's ctrl-build remote answers "start remote run: permission denied"), so no
// session could produce a receipt, and the required PR job does not evaluate witnesses at all
// (DESIGN.md, Reference: building and checks: "Nothing on the required path evaluates a witness").
// What follows is therefore a DECLARED FRONTIER WITH A TRIGGER, not a consumed fact:
//   ENROLLED: two rows, in the two authorities the wet lane's own recipe names
//     (v2.workflow.floor_route_gap chunk_06 header): the `WetScheduledClaim` row of
//     `v2.workflow.local_repo_wet_terminal::local_repo_wet_schedule`, and the
//     `WitnessExclusionRow { classification: LocalRepoWetLane }` of
//     `gunbc.ci.ci_layer_roots::witness_exclusion_frontier` that classifies THIS file out of the
//     hermetic corpus. The schedule projection is checked to carry the identity
//     (`local_repo_wet_scheduled_identities` returns it).
//   NOT YET EVIDENCED: an execution. The trigger that discharges it is the fleet's floor run on a
//     candidate containing this module — the changed-witness lane plans a changed witness module on
//     its commit — and the discharge is that run's own pair of lines: `[local-repo-wet] scheduled=N
//     admitted=N refusals=0` naming this identity, with the standing read
//     `hermetic-route-gap-held-and-wet-passed`. Until a run link carries both, the gate's executing
//     route is a frontier, and this node's counting must say so.
//
// WHY THIS ROUTE AND NOT A HERMETIC ONE: the membership arm reads the PREPARED SUBJECT's git history
// (`origin/main...HEAD`), a MOVING base, so no published `mock_response` can serve it — which is
// precisely why the sibling test.claim.external_model_scope_witness is admitted hermetically (its
// base is the frozen anchor `legacy_manifest_freeze_sha`) while this arm is not. Mocking it would
// satisfy every assertion while the wall the node is paying for (a new dag/extdeps file that joins no
// roster) still ships: the fabricated-plausible-output failure the route-gap notes refuse.
//
// WHICH ARM, AND WHY ONLY THAT ONE (operator decision 2026-11-15, on a measured cost): the live
// claim runs the MEMBERSHIP arm only — the arm that keeps the extdeps population from growing, 0.5 s
// measured locally (blobless clone, 2026-11-15) for its `origin/main...HEAD` read. The freeze and
// remove-only arms read `legacy_manifest_freeze_sha..HEAD`, measured at 61 s for one such read on the
// same checkout, and the CI job budgets are closed to growth (ruling
// `gunbc.design_ruling::ci_job_budgets_closed_to_growth`), so their live reading stays offline. Their
// hermetic cover, cited rather than re-implemented, is
// `test.claim.external_model_scope_witness::manifest_freeze_holds` (same frozen anchor, same
// manifest-row question); the verdict kernels of all three arms carry the mutation controls in
// `test.claim.extdeps_scope_placement_gate_verdict_witness`.

import std.process { ExitSuccess }
import std.types { Bool }
import gunbc.instruments.extdeps_scope_placement_gate {
  scope_placement_change_added_paths,
  scope_placement_membership_verdict,
}

// THE ENROLMENT CLAIM: the gate's own observation builder and the gate's own membership verdict, over
// the prepared subject. Nothing here re-implements an arm: the observation comes from
// `scope_placement_change_added_paths` and the decision from `scope_placement_membership_verdict`, so
// the gate module stays the single authority over what a placement refusal is. A red arrives as the
// gate's located reason, naming the offending path.

test fn the_membership_arm_verdict_passes_on_the_prepared_subject() -> Bool {
  match scope_placement_membership_verdict(observation: scope_placement_change_added_paths()) {
    ExitSuccess => true
    _ => false
  }
}
